  Status: bounded source/manuscript audit; no new mathematical proof. Source
  pin: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>. This is an audit
  of the C11 same-history interfaces, not a claim that C11 or the common
  history is closed.

  <section|Question and conclusion><label|question-and-conclusion>

  Do the existing public-binding, common-funded-history, path-attachment,
  actual-phase-grid, and same-data compiler chapters already derive the exact
  path/clip, <verbatim|Alongside>, inherited-law, and <verbatim|Tissue>
  inputs at the local marked step from one public selected history?

  <strong|Not yet.> The chapters establish the same-history framework and
  several local implications, but the local compiler still assumes a
  same-step receipt that is not produced by the common-history prose. The
  missing edge is a same-data construction of the <verbatim|Seeks> package
  (or an equivalent expanded receipt) for each step of the retained history.
  <verbatim|Tissue> is not an additional analytic obstruction once a
  <verbatim|Lawful> witness with the exact requested parameters is available:
  <verbatim|Tissue.cloth> constructs it. The existence and parameter match of
  that witness are part of the missing binding.

  <section|Exact existing clauses and their
  limits><label|exact-existing-clauses-and-their-limits>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Existing
  prose/source>>|<cell|<strong|What it establishes>>|<cell|<strong|What it
  does not establish>>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|common-funded-history.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:common-funded-history>, together with
  <verbatim|original-history-portfolio-attachment.tex>,
  <verbatim|prop:ex-original-history-attachment>>|<cell|One selected run
  stores one history, schedule, transition/transfer family, and family
  <verbatim|C_R>; its funded continuation acts on those stored objects. The
  finite-volume transfer witnesses and centered service remain on that same
  family. The common-history construction preserves stationary paths below
  the terminal normalization and uses one selected path sequence.>|<cell|It
  is conditional on the funded continuation and the analytic history/path
  suppliers. It does not identify each local <verbatim|Dyed> step's source
  path and clip with the path variables at the C11 attachment interface, or
  construct a local <verbatim|Aff.Alongside>
  witness.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|path-attachment-producer.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:path-attachment-producer>; evidence
  <verbatim|path-attachment-producer-evidence.md>>|<cell|The finite-cutoff
  stationary path construction is detailed once its exact inputs are
  supplied. Its <verbatim|HorizCalc>/<verbatim|pouring> interface quantifies
  over a bed, clip, path, and budget and requires <verbatim|PathData.Bounds>,
  <verbatim|Attached>, metric strip, direct clip bound, floors, sworn
  conditions, and the stationary scene data.>|<cell|Those input records are
  not consequences of finite descending induction or common-history
  attachment. In particular, this producer does not independently supply the
  <verbatim|Alongside> object consumed by the local opacity step. The
  annulus/path-history inputs retained by this chapter remain
  upstream.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|actual-phase-grid-approximants.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:actual-phase-grid-approximants>; evidence
  <verbatim|actual-phase-grid-approximants-evidence.md>>|<cell|Produces
  <verbatim|Origin>, <verbatim|Maker>, and the phase-grid approximants on the
  same selected <verbatim|Makes>, <verbatim|Scrim>, <verbatim|Tabs>, and
  <verbatim|CellHyp> data, with actual finite-volume normalization and all
  required layout types.>|<cell|Its evidence explicitly retains availability
  of those selected inputs. It is not a constructor for <verbatim|Seeks> or
  for the local tube/bed pair.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|actual-local-compiler-handoff.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:actual-local-compiler-handoff>, especially its opening
  interface and final paragraph>|<cell|Given the actual tube, fine
  representation, budget, chart/profiles, path and clip of that
  representation, the local estimates can be assembled on one data set. It
  correctly says the actual <verbatim|Alongside>, inherited-law, path/clip,
  and small-remainder inputs are retained.>|<cell|It does not claim to
  produce these four inputs from the selected public history. Its local
  matrix, marked-density, and reset calculations cannot certify the missing
  history-level receipt.>>|<row|<cell|<verbatim|actual-corrected-body-compiler.tex>,
  <verbatim|sec:actual-corrected-body-compiler>;
  <verbatim|actual-mixed-marked-compiler.tex>>|<cell|Proves the corrected
  alphabet/compiler and its analytic price implications under the actual
  path, clip, law, and marked-data hypotheses.>|<cell|These are consumers.
  They do not turn an abstract local representation into the selected
  history's <verbatim|Dyed> representation, nor produce its path/clip or an
  accompanying tube witness.>>>>>

  The authoritative C11 checklist in <verbatim|handoff/C11.md> names \Pactual
  path/clip/Alongside and inherited-law inputs\Q as items to close, rather
  than listing them as proved. The current local-compiler evidence says these
  same identifications remain explicit. This agrees with the chapter
  statements above; the closure refresh does not infer a proof from record
  names.

  <section|Source-level seam><label|source-level-seam>

  The following immediate declarations were checked in the pinned Lean tree.

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.Seeks> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Opacity/Offers.lean>
    is the exact local package. For a <verbatim|Dyed> object <verbatim|v>,
    teller <verbatim|P>, and scale <verbatim|x>, it contains
    <verbatim|P.Funds S v.things>, the arc identity, the equalities
    <verbatim|v.things.up=v.source.path> and
    <verbatim|v.things.high=v.source.clip>, the retimed threshold and period
    bound, <verbatim|Bid.Larger>, the existential <verbatim|Aff.Alongside H K
    v.things>, an existential <verbatim|v.source.Lawful P.top.width
    P.top.paths \<Gamma\> \<delta\> w> with
    <verbatim|\<Gamma\>\<leq\>betaF(G,retime x,L)^(1/8)> and
    <verbatim|\<delta\>\<leq\>(retime x)^(-1/2)>, and the head, walls,
    beta-band, and flag identities.

    <item><verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Pump.hoops> takes
    <verbatim|Seeks> as an input and upgrades it to <verbatim|Helps>; it
    copies <verbatim|alongside>, <verbatim|law>, and path/clip identities
    into the latter. <verbatim|Pump.vouches> builds <verbatim|Mesa> by
    applying <verbatim|hoops>, but still supplies <verbatim|Seeks> at its
    <verbatim|arrange> field. Thus these declarations are consumers of the
    exact receipt, not a producer of it.

    <item><verbatim|Aff.Alongside A B T>, defined in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/AnalyticNext/CONNECTED_ACTIVITY_BOUNDS/Station.lean>,
    is stronger than a path/clip equality. It requires <verbatim|Attached A
    T.up>, <verbatim|Attached B T.down>, the diagonal identity for
    <verbatim|T.R>, the two-sided roll identity, floor records for both beds
    at the corresponding high/low clips, and sworn conditions for both beds.
    None follows from <verbatim|Seeks.paths> and <verbatim|Seeks.clips>
    alone; <verbatim|Seeks.alongside> is a separate field.

    <item><verbatim|Soft.Tissue R o C L q w>, in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Soft/Tissue.lean>,
    consists of <verbatim|Lawful> for the white representation at the same
    tuple, nonempty moves for every signed/site pair, and the
    <verbatim|Petals R q> regular activity budget.
    <verbatim|Soft.Tissue.cloth> constructs this package directly from
    <verbatim|R.Lawful o C L q w>; <verbatim|Petals.thin> only weakens its
    price parameter in the increasing direction. Therefore, where the
    selected <verbatim|Seeks.law> witness has exactly the consumer's
    <verbatim|(o,C,L,q,w)> tuple, <verbatim|cloth> discharges
    <verbatim|Tissue> without another analytic estimate. A change in the
    tuple, or merely knowing upper bounds on <verbatim|\<Gamma\>,\<delta\>>,
    is not an automatic <verbatim|Tissue> construction; one must state the
    source weakening and check all five parameters.

    <item><verbatim|Soft.Burl.made_soft> consumes a <verbatim|Tissue> input
    for its output representation and proves the pushed density equality. It
    does not produce the original <verbatim|Tissue> or identify its
    representation with the one in the selected history.
    <verbatim|Soft.Bonfire> also explicitly stores <verbatim|Tissue> in its
    per-level <verbatim|Buoyant> data; that constructor is downstream of the
    history-level receipt.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Immediate <verbatim|Seeks> producer and public-route
  boundary><label|immediate-seeks-producer-and-public-route-boundary>

  The source-level search found an actual local constructor, so the earlier
  statement that no inspected source constructs <verbatim|Seeks> must be read
  narrowly: the remaining question is whether its hypotheses are supplied on
  the retained public history. <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.fitPost>
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/PhysicalNext/AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Opacity/Forestage.lean>
  constructs <verbatim|Seeks (tabloid ...) (tell B i) r X> from the same
  <verbatim|B : Binding C>, <verbatim|M : C.Makes>, <verbatim|ShowHours>,
  <verbatim|Marquee>, <verbatim|Corridor>, <verbatim|k\<leq\>N>, and
  <verbatim|Bush> data. Here its <verbatim|tabloid> has source representation
  <verbatim|P>, the tube <verbatim|tunnel B N i p>, and the chart, arc, and
  bed selected in the same course. Its proof fills the receipt as follows:

  <\itemize-dot>
    <item><verbatim|ships B N i p M hs> supplies funding for that tube;
    <verbatim|hP.exactTree> and <verbatim|hP.exactClip> identify its upper
    path and high clip with the source representation. The dressing and
    <verbatim|calendar_warm> provide the arc and flag equalities, while
    <verbatim|Z.great.timing>, <verbatim|B.sized>, and
    <verbatim|ShowHours.yard> provide the retimed threshold, period, and
    support-exponent identities.

    <item>The <verbatim|Aff.Alongside> witness is explicitly assembled from
    the two horizon beds <verbatim|B.world.H N (i+1)> and <verbatim|B.world.H
    N i>; attachments come from <verbatim|B.paths>, the diagonal/roll data
    from <verbatim|B.pays.crossings> and <verbatim|B.pays.stack>, floors from
    <verbatim|B.pays.all>, and sworn conditions from <verbatim|B.sworn>. This
    is a construction of the full two-bed record, not an inference from path
    and clip equalities.

    <item>The inherited-law witness is <verbatim|hP.rated> from
    <verbatim|Bush>, transported across the same-stage identity obtained from
    the corridor plateau and matched to the old-price tuple by
    <verbatim|ShowHours>. The beta-band and walls fields use the
    <verbatim|Bush>/<verbatim|Paint> and <verbatim|bush_prices> receipts.
  </itemize-dot>

  There are two immediate consumers. <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.intoProp>
  in the same file calls <verbatim|fitPost>, obtains the applicable
  <verbatim|Mesa> from <verbatim|Marquee.great.localizes>, and invokes its
  <verbatim|arrange> field at that exact <verbatim|S> and <verbatim|Dyed>
  object. <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.InteractingRank.Soft.lifted> in
  <verbatim|Soft/Bonfire.lean> also calls <verbatim|fitPost> (with the
  neutralized tabloid) and feeds its result to <verbatim|Kraft.prescribes>;
  <verbatim|Soft/Unlid.lean> consumes that result. The only direct call to
  <verbatim|Pump.vouches> found by targeted search is in
  <verbatim|Opacity/Auction.lean> (<verbatim|Pump.billable>), where it
  constructs a <verbatim|Mesa>; this does not independently produce
  <verbatim|Seeks>, but its local <verbatim|hoops>/arrangement consumer
  requires the same kind of local receipt.

  The actual public theorem has a distinct, now precisely identified route.
  <verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean> invokes
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>
  and returns the original <verbatim|Run>, its <verbatim|Campaign>,
  <verbatim|Campaign.Pillars>, funding, and
  <verbatim|ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.Attached>. The selected route's
  <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Campaign.Album.makes> construction
  in <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Shroud/Clan.lean> gives <verbatim|C.Makes>
  on the stamped <verbatim|R.family> from that campaign/history data, when
  this is the family chosen for the local course. But
  <verbatim|constructionRun> does not itself return the extra local
  <verbatim|Binding C>, <verbatim|ShowHours>, <verbatim|Marquee>,
  <verbatim|Corridor>, and <verbatim|Bush> witnesses as fields.
  <verbatim|ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.Attached> records the original
  sheet, quotes, numerical/post-length requests, and native realization; it
  is not itself a <verbatim|Binding C> or <verbatim|fitPost> package. The
  canonical common-history chapters may supply these through their separately
  paid same-history interfaces, but a same-object substitution from their
  exact output to every argument of <verbatim|fitPost> is not established by
  the constructor statements read here. Thus the remaining join is narrower:
  bind the selected public run's retained <verbatim|R.family> and funded
  history to one <verbatim|Binding C>, <verbatim|ShowHours>,
  <verbatim|Marquee>, <verbatim|Corridor>, and <verbatim|Bush> on the same
  <verbatim|C>, <verbatim|N>, and indices, then apply <verbatim|fitPost> and
  the relevant <verbatim|arrange>. There is no need to reprove the
  <verbatim|Alongside> field construction inside <verbatim|fitPost> once
  those inputs are bound.

  If the actual course instead supplies an arbitrary <verbatim|Dyed v>, the
  precise correspondence needed is an equality/transport identifying it with
  the <verbatim|Forestage.tabloid> on the same source, tube, chart, and
  token; no arbitrary- <verbatim|Dyed> generalization was found. The separate
  full stationary <verbatim|PathData.Bounds>/<verbatim|Attached> and
  <verbatim|HorizCalc> gates remain their own C11 path producer; this audit
  does not conflate them with local <verbatim|Aff.Alongside>.

  <section|Reads and checks><label|reads-and-checks>

  Read-only sources: parent <verbatim|handoff/C11.md>, the C11 block of
  <verbatim|handoff/package-plan.json>, parent
  <verbatim|common-funded-history.tex>, <verbatim|original-history-portfolio-attachment.tex>,
  <verbatim|path-attachment-producer.tex>,
  <verbatim|actual-phase-grid-approximants.tex>,
  <verbatim|actual-local-compiler-handoff.tex>,
  <verbatim|actual-corrected-body-compiler.tex>, and
  <verbatim|actual-mixed-marked-compiler.tex>; their corresponding listed
  evidence files; and pinned source files <verbatim|Opacity/Offers.lean>,
  <verbatim|Opacity/Gush.lean>, <verbatim|AnalyticNext/CONNECTED_ACTIVITY_BOUNDS/Station.lean>,
  <verbatim|Soft/Tissue.lean>, <verbatim|Soft/Burl.lean>,
  <verbatim|Soft/Bonfire.lean>, <verbatim|Soft/Unlid.lean>,
  <verbatim|Opacity/Forestage.lean>, <verbatim|Opacity/Auction.lean>,
  <verbatim|Opacity/Pergola.lean>, <verbatim|Opacity/Epoch.lean>,
  <verbatim|AFTERNOON_INTERACTING_RANK_COMPARISON/Leashes.lean>,
  <verbatim|RANK_COVARIANCE_ATLAS/Consumer.lean>,
  <verbatim|Source/Construction.lean>, <verbatim|FullVolume/Shroud/Clan.lean>,
  <verbatim|RG17/Joint.lean>, <verbatim|Independent/ConstructionRun.lean>,
  <verbatim|Integration/ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.lean>, and
  <verbatim|Integration/NativePreselectedPostnumericPeriodRun.lean>. Targeted
  <verbatim|sed>/<verbatim|rg> inspections only, including <verbatim|rg -n
  "Pump\\\\.vouches\|vouches\|fitPost\|intoProp\|constructionRun\|extractible17">
  over the named source subtrees; no whole-tree traversal, Lean edit, or
  build. This audit file is the only intended output of the refresh task.
  <verbatim|git diff --no-index --check /dev/null
  blueprint/units/YM-000026/lattice-history-closure-refresh.md> emitted no
  whitespace diagnostics (exit status 1 because the file is new).
  <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py> was attempted; it could not
  run because this isolated clone lacks the coordinator-owned
  <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>. No TeX or Lean build was
  run.

  <section|Subsequent narrowed result><label|subsequent-narrowed-result>

  The later <verbatim|selected-course-binding.tex> and its evidence supersede
  this early frontier: Run.bought supplies Binding on literal R.family;
  generic Paid weakening is proved. The source's internal franchise receipt
  is not exported for an already fixed R, but that alone is not a new
  analytic obstruction. The next comparison must use the actual exported
  Chateau rated/warrant/market outputs where sufficient, then match the exact
  local consumer. Do not impose a stronger raw-receipt task without showing
  it is required. Exact review findings are in reviews/.

